    ":question/id": "418cd3d5-ecfd-5690-a4c6-98dd1a3d29e8",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-122768",
    ":question/problem": "![](images/b7/b7e72ce1ab38408f04f3b8d5a228ec0a3632c60086ef0a7abeb7e18af3002e6b.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5.\n$$"
  },
