    ":question/id": "87f72e02-2150-54e7-a38e-3cb9d2a4dc70",
    ":question/problem": "![Semicircle of radius 2 with counterclockwise arrows](images/24/244e830a32373fc20379f9b55650452c77e1a422ce5ee9456007cdac0d0daebc.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the semicircular arc of radius $2$ shown above, traversed once counterclockwise.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length equals the length $L$ of the path:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is half of a circle of radius $2$, so\n\n$$\nL=\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi r)=\\pi(2)=2\\pi.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=2\\pi.\n$$\n\nOnly the curved arc is traversed; the radius drawn as a dashed guide is not part of $C$."
  },
